The game's core ideas (creating your own vehicle and then fighting with it) are wonderful, and could have lead to endless hours of entertainment. However, the developers became very greedy, and have practically destroyed the game. It almost requires monetary investment to progress in the game, and gives players who pay their way to victory a sharp edge. It would have been much more desirable if the game was more sandbox-like, such as Space Engineers. This is not the case, instead of having certain effects negate others (eg. adding armor increases weight, and makes you less mobile) and allowing users to create ships with whatever properties they wish, the game has a complexity limit, much like Spore. As the player progresses, they gain more complexity allowance and are moved to fight with other ships. You can pay money to progress in the game, and purchasing a 'premium' membership (which, unlike Team Fortress 2, must be renewed). I would not have a problem paying an up-front fee for this game, even if it were above what most games in this category cost, but will not invest a penny in the game because the benefits don't come anywhere near the costs.
In conclusion, I would only reccomend this game because it is free. You'll get a few hours of entertainment out of it, but I would save my hard earned dollars for games that center around the gameplay experience, not the amount of money the developer can rake (
) out of their customers.

